Z||000000||Uaana||01-03-2001||02:35 AM||||o.k. basics. 87 GT Everything stock except the plug wires. (6 mos old)<BR>Car has been running rich. (cracked manifold)<BR>Problem. Drove to work tonight no prob. <BR>Get in car no start. It coughed a couple of times but that's it. Almost sounds flooded.<BR>Had someone crank it and all I could see was some heavy arcing off of the coil..<BR>Suggestions?<BR>Please it's stuck at work and I can't afford to have it towed 30mi to screw with it at home.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||01-03-2001||02:58 AM||||Bad ignition coil, and/or ignition module come to mind.. I have my old coil that still works if you need it, I think..<P>Could it have just gotten really wet somehow?  That would cause the arcing and also a no-start..||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-03-2001||07:56 PM||||Arcing off coil could be bad cap/rotor, bad wires or bad coil. 6 month old wires can be bad. especially some of the off brand stuff. HEI distributor caps are great for cooking out the center contact to the rotor. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Uaana||01-04-2001||01:37 AM||||Thanks guys.<BR>Went and got new pickup coil, ing coil, cap and rotor.<BR>Went out at lunch to start trading parts.<P>Did you know that the D@#n mounting braket for the coil is rivited onto the damn thing!!!<BR>Or is this a Fiero specific item that i need?||||reg||8
Z||000004||mrfiero||01-04-2001||01:53 AM||||You will need to drill out the old rivets and attach the new coil with the screws/nuts provided in the kit.<P>These coils were used in a variety of GM vehicles, so they come without brackets. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||01-04-2001||02:31 AM||||My old coil (which looked original) used some really small (6mm I think) nuts and bolts to attach it..  while you're in there, I would take out the heat sheild for the coil.  Looks a lot cleaner without it in there, and makes it a bunch easier to work on the coil.  I took mine off when I changed it and haven't had any problems since.||||reg||
Z||000006||Uaana||01-04-2001||04:13 AM||||Thanks again! Don't you guys ever sleep?<BR>And I would have figured this out if I had actually read those pesky instruction things included with the parts. <BR>Guess this is what I get for being in a hurry and trying to work on my car at work.<P>Funny thing though you should have seen the looks I got from the collection of computer geeks I work with.. "work on a car and get like dirty???"<BR>Thats what mechanics are for..<BR> ||||reg||1
